w a W4 or a W1, I can form a chow with W2-3-4 or W1-2-3. But since I have to discard one tile, maybe W9 is the best choice.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Discarding W9 maintains the potential for two chows (T4-5-6 and B5-6-7) and a pair of J3s, while removing an unconnected terminal tile that doesn't contribute to melds. This leaves the hand with better structure for completing the required four melds.\n\nReason: By discarding W9, the hand retains critical chows in T and B suits and the J3 pair. The remaining tiles (W2, W3, T2, F3, F4) offer flexibility for forming additional melds if the right tiles are drawn, such as W4 for a chow or another J3 for a pung. This move optimizes the chance of completing a valid hand with higher scoring potential.\n\nAnswer: Play W9"}
